  ChatGPT page reports `ready` with an inactive Send button (read-only).
- Reworked ChatGPT answer anchoring to track optional logical DOM turn IDs
  and handle a virtualized replacement even without an increased message count.
- Added a conservative count fallback: if a replacement cannot be identified
  reliably, timeout rather than accept a possibly stale response.
- Completion evidence remains scoped to the new answer; old Copy controls do
  not count, and pending/Stop indicators block premature return.
- Added six unit tests and two optional real Chromium HTML-fixture tests.
- Added docs/turn-identity.md. No production ChatGPT submission was tested.

