# OpenAgent — Change Log

## 0.4.5 — 2026-10-20
- Fixed Firefox cookie migration failing with Playwright's `Cookie should have a
  valid expires` error when Firefox stores extremely distant future expiries.
- Cap only oversized future expiry timestamps to Playwright's year-9999 maximum
  (253402300799 seconds); invalid/expired values remain excluded.
- Convert Playwright cookie-insertion exceptions into sanitized browser-session
  errors so the CLI does not print driver tracebacks or authentication material.
- Added SQLite regression tests for int64 expiry sentinels, browser-error tests,
  and optional real-Chromium verification with synthetic cookies.
- Login after import remains unverified; no password access or security bypass.

## 0.4.4 — 2026-10-20
- Added read-only browser-profile discovery for Firefox (profiles.ini), Chrome,
  Edge, and existing OpenAgent-managed persistent profiles.
- Added explicit `browser session import-firefox --profile ... --site chatgpt.com --yes`
  to import only nonexpired, nonpartitioned ChatGPT site cookies from an enumerated
  Firefox profile to the selected OpenAgent persistent browser backend.
- No saved passwords, Google-domain cookies, session JSON export, or automatic login;
  successful cookie import is not proof of an authenticated ChatGPT session.
- Added backend-scoped cookie injection guards and offline SQLite tests.
- Added a short Windows Playwright subprocess-shutdown drain (best-effort);
  Windows Ctrl+C behavior still needs a real-machine check.

## 0.4.3 — 2026-10-20
- Identified the Windows `ui_changed` root cause from a user-provided screenshot:
  the ChatGPT homepage rendered normally but was logged out, showing visible
  "Log in" buttons that the selector did not recognize.
- Updated the experimental ChatGPT public-UI selector candidates for semantic
  login buttons/links, anonymous composer, and send controls.
- UI diagnostics now check multiple candidate matches when the first matching
  element is hidden (mobile/desktop duplicate controls).
- Added a synthetic logged-out HTML fixture and regression tests verifying
  `login_required` takes precedence over composer readiness, without submitting.
- No automatic login, credential copying, provider-challenge bypass, or live
  ChatGPT message submission; browser account authentication remains separate.


## 0.4.2 — 2026-10-20
- Confirmed from Windows logs: authenticated /v1/models returns HTTP 200; 78 tests
  passed, but ChatGPT UI diagnostics found no visible controls.
- Added `browser chatgpt-status --wait-seconds N` (default 8, max 30) to wait
  for SPA hydration before classifying a missing composer as `ui_changed`.
- Extended `--details` with a safe DOM-shape summary (load state, main/body
  presence and control counts). No page text, URL path, cookies, tokens or
  account information is captured or printed.
- Added explicit opt-in `--screenshot PATH.png`, locally saved with no
  overwrite. The screenshot can contain private account/chat information;
  review locally before sharing.
- Added offline regression tests for hydration delay, missing UI, error
  sanitization, explicit screenshot saving and no-overwrite behavior.
- No live ChatGPT adapter verification or authentication workaround.

## 0.4.1 — 2026-10-20
- Added local-only `api-check` that distinguishes unreachable server, 401 token mismatch,
  and successful authorized model discovery without printing secrets.
- Added `browser chatgpt-status --details` to show read-only selector visibility
  and whether the browser remained on chatgpt.com (no page text or credentials).
- Documented two independent PowerShell terminals, environment variable scope,
  and rebuilding `$headers` after setting the API token.
- Added targeted regression tests. Live ChatGPT website compatibility is unverified.


## 0.4.0 — 2026-10-20
- Added opt-in `chatgpt-web/default` public UI preview behind `--enable-chatgpt-web`;
  browser profile selection is inherited from v0.2.1. No automated login.
- Added ChatGPT-specific DOM completion requiring a *new*, completed assistant
  turn and no active generation or pending state; stale copy buttons ignored.
- Added `browser chatgpt-status` for read-only readiness/permission diagnostics
  and `/openagent/providers/chatgpt-web/diagnostics` when registered.
- Added account-capable HTTP protection: `OPENAGENT_API_TOKEN` is required
  with `--enable-chatgpt-web`, even on loopback.
- Added safe adapter error codes and server-lifespan browser teardown.
- Added injected ChatGPT-shaped HTML fixture (real Chromium) and offline tests;
  optional DOM tests also discover the selected portable Chromium executable
  using a disposable test profile, without accessing the user's login data.
- 72 tests passed on Linux; Windows runtime and live ChatGPT behavior unverified.
- No verified ChatGPT model switching, projects, file transfer, native tools or streaming.

## 0.3.0 — 2026-10-20
- Added selector-driven UI diagnostics with structured visual states and no
  credential/cookie extraction; CLI `browser diagnose`.
- Added experimental `BrowserUIProvider` and `BrowserSiteProfile` with
  full ordered JSON transcript preservation, response anchoring, stable
  completion evidence, and no automatic resubmission after uncertainty.
- Added offline local HTML chat fixture and loopback-only `browser ui-test`.
- Added tests for authentication markers, completion indicators, timeouts,
  cancellation, stale markers, and a real Chromium DOM test using injected HTML.
- Left live model registration, provider authentication, and native tool-call
  translation unimplemented; no new public website was automated.

## 0.2.2 — 2026-10-20
- Fixed Windows discovery fixture isolation: when paths/environment are injected,
  discovery no longer reads real system Registry installations.
- Removed duplicate portable Chrome/Chromium candidate rows for one executable.
- Replaced `asyncio.to_thread(input)` in interactive `browser open` with
  cancellable nonblocking console polling; single Ctrl+C requests clean shutdown.
- Added regression tests for simulated Windows discovery, interactive Enter,
  Ctrl+C, and browser-context cleanup.
- Documented Google's automated-browser login restriction and the Chromium
  download CDN region error. Neither is bypassed by OpenAgent.

## 0.2.1 — 2026-10-20
- Added read-only cross-platform system browser discovery and matching Playwright
  Chromium/Firefox cache detection with explicit portable-path scanning.
- Added `browser select`, persisted backend choice, and `--browser-path` folder/exe
  support for a manually downloaded Chromium, Chrome or Edge executable.
- Added backend selection for Playwright Firefox with isolated persistent profile.
- Added `browser open --url` for user-driven one-time login in a reusable profile.
- Documented that ordinary Firefox and its existing logged-in personal profile
  cannot automatically be reused by Playwright, and CDP is Chromium-only.
- Added offline Windows discovery/selection/backend tests.
- Centralized API version from package version to prevent drift.

## 0.2.0 — 2026-10-18
- Added optional Playwright Browser Manager and separate backend implementation.
- Supports `persistent` (dedicated profile) and `cdp` (local existing browser)
  modes; no automated login or site-specific scraping.
- Added explicit request-tab ownership, origin restriction, navigation timeout,
  tab cap, state reporting, failure cleanup, and disconnected/restart behavior.
- Added `openagent browser probe` with visible/headless and CDP options.
- Changed the default port from 8765 to Windows-tested 12321; added
  `OPENAGENT_PORT`, `--strict-port`, and port availability fallback.
- Added browser-specific documentation and offline lifecycle/backend tests.
- Kept command execution outside of the bridge and model adapters mock-only.

## 0.1.1 — 2026-10-18
- Added root-level TODO, PROFILE, CHANGES and .gitignore.
- Corrected Windows PowerShell environment instructions.
- Updated Python compatibility requirement to 3.10+ and development
  dependency constraints.
- Added package/API version regression tests.

## 0.1.0 — 2026-10-18
- Added FastAPI-compatible bridge, mock provider and capabilities.
- Added OAP/1 validation and a durable SQLite session journal.
- Added basic synthetic SSE and API/session tests.

## Known limitations
- Browser probes and backend ownership are tested with deterministic fakes;
  no live Chromium/browser probe was executed by this package's release tests.
- Live ChatGPT UI interaction has not been verified; the preview may report
  `ui_changed` or `generation_timeout`. No Claude/DeepSeek provider yet.
- No native streaming, file transfer, or tool executor implemented.
